CENSUS {"python": "/oscar/scratch/sboughan/venvs/se7-craftax/bin/python", "registry": ["Acrobot", "AntmazeGiantNavigate", "AntmazeGiantStitch", "AntmazeLargeExplore", "AntmazeLargeNavigate", "AntmazeLargeStitch", "AntmazeMediumExplore", "AntmazeMediumNavigate", "AntmazeMediumStitch", "AntmazeTeleportExplore", "AntmazeTeleportNavigate", "AntmazeTeleportStitch", "BabyAIGoToLocal", "CartPole", "CraftaxClassic", "CraftaxFull", "Crafter", "Highway", "HumanoidmazeGiantNavigate", "HumanoidmazeGiantStitch", "HumanoidmazeLargeNavigate", "HumanoidmazeLargeStitch", "HumanoidmazeMediumNavigate", "HumanoidmazeMediumStitch", "Intersection", "Merge", "MiniGridDoorKey", "MiniGridEmpty", "MiniGridFourRooms", "MiniGridKeyCorridor", "MiniGridLavaCrossing", "MiniGridPOVFetch", "MiniHack", "MountainCar", "MountainCarContinuous", "MujocoInvertedDoublePendulum", "MujocoInvertedPendulum", "MujocoPusher", "MujocoReacher", "OGBCube", "OGBScene", "Parking", "Pendulum", "Piecewise", "PiecewiseZones", "PointMazeLarge", "PointMazeMedium", "PointMazeOpen", "PointMazeUMaze", "PointmazeGiantNavigate", "PointmazeGiantStitch", "PointmazeLargeNavigate", "PointmazeLargeStitch", "PointmazeMediumNavigate", "PointmazeMediumStitch", "PointmazeTeleportNavigate", "PointmazeTeleportStitch", "PushT", "Racetrack", "Roundabout", "SimplePointMaze", "TwoRoom", "TwoRoomTarget"], "n": 63, "import_errors": {"carracing": "ImportError: CarRacing-v3 cannot be reset and rendered: DependencyNotInstalled: Box2D is not installed, you can install it by run `pip install swig` followed by `pip install \"gymnasium[box2d]\"`. This env needs BOTH `box2d-py` (for the simulator that produces its states) and `pygame` (for the reference renderer parity is measured against); `pip install swig` then `pip install \"gymnasium[box2d]\"`.", "dmcontrol": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'dm_control'", "fetch": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mujoco'", "griddly": "ImportError: griddly is not importable (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'griddly'). The atlas is composed of tiles griddly's own Vulkan renderer draws, so there is no degraded mode. `pip install griddly==1.6.7` \u2014 the only release, from 2023-03-15; upstream's last commit is 2024-04-07 and there is no successor.", "humanoidbench": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mujoco'", "jumanji": "ImportError: the Jumanji family builds its per-pixel atlas by CALLING the official matplotlib viewer, so it cannot render without the reference package: missing jumanji. The envs were measured in /mnt/vast/home/randall.balestriero/venvs/se-jumanji, built with a CLEAN `python -m venv` \u2014 a --system-site-packages venv breaks jax's CUDA plugin discovery. See docs/research/jumanji.md", "lunarlander": "ImportError: LunarLander-v3 cannot be reset and rendered: DependencyNotInstalled: Box2D is not installed, you can install it by run `pip install swig` followed by `pip install \"gymnasium[box2d]\"`. This env needs BOTH `box2d-py` (for the simulator that produces its states) and `pygame` (for the reference renderer parity is measured against); `pip install swig` then `pip install \"gymnasium[box2d]\"`.", "metaworld": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mujoco'", "overcooked": "ImportError: jaxmarl is not importable (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'jaxmarl'). The atlas IS jaxmarl's own `_render_tile` output \u2014 nothing here re-derives it \u2014 so there is no degraded mode. `pip install jaxmarl` (measured against jaxmarl 0.1.0 / jax 0.4.38) INTO A CLEAN VENV: a `python -m venv --system-site-packages` venv breaks jax's CUDA plugin discovery.", "pgx": "ImportError: the PGX family needs pgx (which brings jax), resvg_py and Pillow, and this interpreter cannot provide them: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pgx'. The envs were measured in /mnt/vast/home/randall.balestriero/venvs/se-pgx, built with a CLEAN `python -m venv` -- NOT --system-site-packages, which breaks jax's CUDA plugin discovery. See docs/research/pgx.md", "procgen": "ImportError: procgen is not installed; `pip install procgen` provides both the assets this renderer packs and the reference env parity is measured against", "robocasa": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mujoco'", "sokoban": "ImportError: gym-sokoban is not installed. The seven 16x16 tile images ARE this env -- the frame is a gather from them and nothing here re-derives them -- so there is no degraded mode to fall back to. `pip install gym-sokoban`."}, "file": "/oscar/scratch/sboughan/se8/cert/stable_envs/__init__.py", "declarations": {"CartPole": {"name": "cartpole", "reference_id": "CartPole-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "", "state_dim": 2, "default_size": 600, "state_names": ["x", "theta"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "CartPole", "module": "stable_envs.envs.classic_control", "doc": "CartPole-v1. Render state ``[x, theta]`` \u2014 2 of the observation's 4 dims.\n\nDraw order, from the source: cart quad, pole quad, axle disc, then ``hline`` for the track, which\nis painted LAST and therefore over the cart. The cart is axis-aligned, so its ``aapolygon`` takes\nSDL_gfx's solid ``hline``/``vline`` short-circuit and is not anti-aliased at all; only the pole is.\n\n``step`` takes 2 discrete actions \u2014 0 push left, 1 push right \u2014 as one float per environment,\nfloored. Dynamical state ``[x, x_dot, theta, theta_dot]``, Euler at ``tau = 0.02``; tracks the\nreference to **4.4e-14 over 100 steps, 1.1e-16 after one**.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["gfxdraw"]}, "Pendulum": {"name": "pendulum", "reference_id": "Pendulum-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "", "state_dim": 2, "default_size": 500, "state_names": ["theta", "torque"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "Pendulum", "module": "stable_envs.envs.classic_control", "doc": "Pendulum-v1. Render state ``[theta, torque]``.\n\n``torque`` is ``last_u``: not part of the observation, but it is drawn, so it is part of the render\nstate. See the module docstring for why it reduces to a 228-entry sprite table and why ``u = 0``\nneeds no separate flag.\n\n``step`` takes one CONTINUOUS torque in [-2, 2]. Dynamical state ``[theta, theta_dot, torque]``, and\nstepping is what makes the third render dimension move on its own: the torque a policy asks for is\nthe torque that gets drawn. Tracks the reference to **2.8e-13 over 100 steps, 2.2e-16 after one**.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["gfxdraw"]}, "Acrobot": {"name": "acrobot", "reference_id": "Acrobot-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "", "state_dim": 2, "default_size": 500, "state_names": ["theta1", "theta2"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "Acrobot", "module": "stable_envs.envs.classic_control", "doc": "Acrobot-v1. Render state ``[theta1, theta2]`` \u2014 2 of the observation's 6 dims.\n\nTwo traps in the source, both silent. ``xys = np.array([[0,0], p1, p2])[:, ::-1]`` **swaps x and\ny**, so link 2 hangs off ``(p1_y, p1_x)``; and ``p2`` is computed but never drawn, because only two\n``thetas`` are zipped against three points. The ground rule is ``pygame.draw.line``, which\nTRUNCATES its float y (363.6364 -> row 363) \u2014 rounding puts the whole line one row off, 1000 px a\nframe, which looks like a rasterizer bug rather than a coordinate one.\n\n``step`` takes 3 discrete actions \u2014 torque -1, 0, +1 \u2014 as one floored float. Dynamical state\n``[theta1, theta2, dtheta1, dtheta2]``, one RK4 step at ``dt = 0.2``; tracks the reference to\n**4.4e-13 over 100 steps, 1.1e-16 after one**. The widest spread in the family and the fewest\nbit-identical steps (15.4%), which is what a chaotic double pendulum is supposed to do to two\ntrajectories that started one ulp apart.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["gfxdraw"]}, "MountainCar": {"name": "mountain-car", "reference_id": "MountainCar-v0", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "", "state_dim": 1, "default_size": 600, "state_names": ["position"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "MountainCar", "module": "stable_envs.envs.classic_control", "doc": "MountainCar-v0. Render state ``[position]`` \u2014 one number for a 400x600 frame.\n\nThe terrain is 99 ``pygame.draw.aalines`` segments, a sub-pixel AA path unrelated to gfxdraw's and\nnot reimplemented; it is also a constant of the environment rather than of the state, so it is\nrasterised once by pygame and cached. That is exact by construction and free per frame. Everything\nthe state moves \u2014 the car quad and its two wheels \u2014 is pure gfxdraw and exact by the rules in\n``render/gfxdraw``. The flag is drawn AFTER the car in the reference, so it cannot join the baked\nlayer; it is gfxdraw too, so it does not need to.\n\n``step`` takes 3 discrete actions \u2014 0 push left, 1 coast, 2 push right \u2014 as one floored float.\nDynamical state ``[position, velocity]``; tracks the reference to **3.3e-16 over 100 steps,\n5.4e-20 after one**, the tightest in the family because one step is three float64 operations and a\ncosine.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["gfxdraw"]}, "MountainCarContinuous": {"name": "mountain-car-continuous", "reference_id": "MountainCarContinuous-v0", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "", "state_dim": 1, "default_size": 600, "state_names": ["position"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "MountainCarContinuous", "module": "stable_envs.envs.classic_control", "doc": "MountainCarContinuous-v0. Nearly two envs for the price of one \u2014 but not quite.\n\n``continuous_mountain_car.render`` is byte-identical to ``mountain_car.render`` apart from one\ncomment (checked by diffing the two sources), which makes it very tempting to reuse the renderer\nunchanged. That is wrong by 23,984 pixels across 64 frames, because the flag is drawn from\n``self.goal_position`` and the two envs do not agree on it: **0.45 here, 0.5 for MountainCar-v0**,\nwith a source comment attributing the difference to a third-party port. Identical draw code over a\ndifferent constant is exactly the class of error a \"looks the same\" check misses and a pixel diff\ncatches immediately.\n\nThe same trap runs through the physics, one level deeper: ``step`` here takes one CONTINUOUS force\nin [-1, 1] scaled by ``power``, and it computes in **float32** where MountainCar-v0 computes in\nfloat64 (see ``_dynamics``). Seeded from a state the reference has already stored, agreement is\n**exact \u2014 exact_frac 1.0, max deviation 0.0 over 16 x 100 steps**; seeded from a freshly reset\nfloat64 state the reference's own first step is in a different dtype regime and the trajectory\ndiffers by up to one float32 ulp of position (1.2e-07).", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["gfxdraw"]}, "CraftaxClassic": {"name": "craftax-classic", "reference_id": "Craftax-Classic-Pixels-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "Measured on 64 sampled states at 7 px and 16 px, over the WHOLE observation -- the 7x9 world window and the 2-row inventory strip -- and over the whole day cycle: 18 night rows (light_level < 0.5, noise field drawn), 29 dusk rows (0.5 <= light < 1, lit but noise-free) and 17 daylight rows, sleeping rows throughout. Against craftax 1.6.1 under jax 0.11.1 with jax_threefry_partitionable at its default True: 100% of all pixels exact in every band, max abs diff 0. The claim is a UINT8 claim and deliberately not a float one, because the reference does not have one float value to be equal to: under jax.jit XLA fuses its arithmetic differently and it disagrees with its own un-jitted self by up to 1.5e-05, which is invisible in uint8 by day and visible wherever the picture is compressed towards one value, which the sleep desaturation and the night blend both do. Against the JITTED reference this renderer is 99.7854% (7 px) and 99.7225% (16 px) of pixels exact with max abs diff 1 ON THIS POOL, where every differing pixel was on a sleeping row; independent review found the jitted reference differing on an awake row at light_level 0.49999997, so any LIT row can straddle and the sleeping rows are only the commonest case. reference_env therefore returns the un-jitted function, which is the renderer as written. jax is a declared reference version because jax_threefry_partitionable selects between two threefry counter layouts that agree on 0 of 448 draws, and the night noise field is drawn from one of them.", "state_dim": 149, "default_size": 16, "state_names": ["block_r0c0", "block_r0c1", "block_r0c2", "block_r0c3", "block_r0c4", "block_r0c5", "block_r0c6", "block_r0c7", "block_r0c8", "block_r1c0", "block_r1c1", "block_r1c2", "block_r1c3", "block_r1c4", "block_r1c5", "block_r1c6", "block_r1c7", "block_r1c8", "block_r2c0", "block_r2c1", "block_r2c2", "block_r2c3", "block_r2c4", "block_r2c5", "block_r2c6", "block_r2c7", "block_r2c8", "block_r3c0", "block_r3c1", "block_r3c2", "block_r3c3", "block_r3c4", "block_r3c5", "block_r3c6", "block_r3c7", "block_r3c8", "block_r4c0", "block_r4c1", "block_r4c2", "block_r4c3", "block_r4c4", "block_r4c5", "block_r4c6", "block_r4c7", "block_r4c8", "block_r5c0", "block_r5c1", "block_r5c2", "block_r5c3", "block_r5c4", "block_r5c5", "block_r5c6", "block_r5c7", "block_r5c8", "block_r6c0", "block_r6c1", "block_r6c2", "block_r6c3", "block_r6c4", "block_r6c5", "block_r6c6", "block_r6c7", "block_r6c8", "mob_r0c0", "mob_r0c1", "mob_r0c2", "mob_r0c3", "mob_r0c4", "mob_r0c5", "mob_r0c6", "mob_r0c7", "mob_r0c8", "mob_r1c0", "mob_r1c1", "mob_r1c2", "mob_r1c3", "mob_r1c4", "mob_r1c5", "mob_r1c6", "mob_r1c7", "mob_r1c8", "mob_r2c0", "mob_r2c1", "mob_r2c2", "mob_r2c3", "mob_r2c4", "mob_r2c5", "mob_r2c6", "mob_r2c7", "mob_r2c8", "mob_r3c0", "mob_r3c1", "mob_r3c2", "mob_r3c3", "mob_r3c4", "mob_r3c5", "mob_r3c6", "mob_r3c7", "mob_r3c8", "mob_r4c0", "mob_r4c1", "mob_r4c2", "mob_r4c3", "mob_r4c4", "mob_r4c5", "mob_r4c6", "mob_r4c7", "mob_r4c8", "mob_r5c0", "mob_r5c1", "mob_r5c2", "mob_r5c3", "mob_r5c4", "mob_r5c5", "mob_r5c6", "mob_r5c7", "mob_r5c8", "mob_r6c0", "mob_r6c1", "mob_r6c2", "mob_r6c3", "mob_r6c4", "mob_r6c5", "mob_r6c6", "mob_r6c7", "mob_r6c8", "player_facing", "inv_health", "inv_food", "inv_drink", "inv_energy", "inv_sapling", "inv_wood", "inv_stone", "inv_coal", "inv_iron", "inv_diamond", "inv_wood_pickaxe", "inv_stone_pickaxe", "inv_iron_pickaxe", "inv_wood_sword", "inv_stone_sword", "inv_iron_sword", "is_sleeping", "light_level", "rng_half0", "rng_half1", "rng_half2", "rng_half3"], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "CraftaxClassic", "module": "stable_envs.envs.craftax", "doc": "Craftax Classic: a 7x9 block window, the player, one mob per tile, and the inventory strip.", "has_step": false, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["prng"]}, "CraftaxFull": {"name": "craftax-full", "reference_id": "Craftax-Pixels-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "Measured on the frozen Step-7 corpus at 10 px (the registered observation) and 16 px, over the WHOLE observation -- the 9x11 world window and the 4-row inventory strip -- and over all five cost bands: level 0 at full daylight, level 0 at dusk, level 0 at night (the noise field drawn), levels 1-8 fully lit, and levels 1-8 in darkness, with sleeping rows throughout. Against craftax 1.6.1 under jax 0.11.1 with jax_threefry_partitionable at its default True and do_night_noise at its default True: 100% of all pixels exact, max abs diff 0. The claim is a UINT8 claim and deliberately not a float one, because the reference does not have one float value to be equal to: under jax.jit XLA fuses its arithmetic differently and it disagrees with its own un-jitted self by up to 1.53e-05, which is invisible in uint8 on a fully lit frame and not invisible wherever the picture is compressed towards one value -- which the light_map multiply, the night blend and the sleep halving all do. On a 49-state phase-0 pool 48 of 49 jitted frames were uint8-identical to the un-jitted ones and one differed on 0.0023% of pixels by 1. reference_env therefore returns the un-jitted function, which is the renderer as written. jax is a declared reference version because jax_threefry_partitionable selects between two threefry counter layouts that agree on 0 of 448 draws, and the night noise field is drawn from one of them.", "state_dim": 544, "default_size": 10, "state_names": ["block_r0c0", "block_r0c1", "block_r0c2", "block_r0c3", "block_r0c4", "block_r0c5", "block_r0c6", "block_r0c7", "block_r0c8", "block_r0c9", "block_r0c10", "block_r1c0", "block_r1c1", "block_r1c2", "block_r1c3", "block_r1c4", "block_r1c5", "block_r1c6", "block_r1c7", "block_r1c8", "block_r1c9", "block_r1c10", "block_r2c0", "block_r2c1", "block_r2c2", "block_r2c3", "block_r2c4", "block_r2c5", "block_r2c6", "block_r2c7", "block_r2c8", "block_r2c9", "block_r2c10", "block_r3c0", "block_r3c1", "block_r3c2", "block_r3c3", "block_r3c4", "block_r3c5", "block_r3c6", "block_r3c7", "block_r3c8", "